        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Excuse My French, Pop That, Hold You Down\n- People: French Montana, Machine Gun Kelly, Richard Colson Baker, MGK, Diddy, Nicki Minaj, Drake, Ace Hood, Lil Wayne, Birdman, The Weeknd, Rick Ross, 2 Chainz, Max B, Ne-Yo, Raekwon, Scarface, Snoop Dogg, Lee on the Beats, DJ Khaled, Bkorn\n- Roles: American rapper, actor, producer\n- Places: Cleveland, Ohio\n\nFacts:\n- Richard Colson Baker was born on April 22, 1990, and he is better known by the stage names MGK and Machine Gun Kelly.\n- Machine Gun Kelly is an American rapper and actor from Cleveland, Ohio.\n- Excuse My French is the debut studio album by American rapper French Montana.\n- Excuse My French features guest appearances from Diddy, Nicki Minaj, Drake, Ace Hood, Lil Wayne, Birdman, The Weeknd, Rick Ross, 2 Chainz, Max B, Ne-Yo, Machine Gun Kelly, Raekwon, Scarface, and Snoop Dogg.\n- Pop That was released as the first single from Excuse My French in 2013.\n- Pop That features guest appearances from Rick Ross, Drake, and Lil Wayne.\n- Lee on the Beats is best known for producing French Montana’s Pop That.\n- Lee on the Beats co-produced DJ Khaled’s Hold You Down with his production partner Bkorn.",
